in the right side of his face. Sergeant Reed sustained two deep lacerations near his ear. Julian was admitted to the surgical ward of Canberra Hospital for an accidental self-inflicted gash in his hand. Sergeant Reed's wounds were non-life-threatening, and he fully recovered. On his release from hospital, Julian was charged with three offenses, malicious wounding, assault-occasioning actual bodily harm, and assault. He was given two options, suspension from the Army until the court hearing, or resign

