00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:52.000
fence and emerged on the eastern edge of Hoddle Street. Pairs of headlights glistened and passed by as Julian crept along the darkened side of the road. He knelt down into some shrubbery, biting himself from view. He positioned himself facing the oncoming traffic, raised his shotgun, and pulled the trigger. One of the first bullets struck the windscreen of a car carrying Alan Dury and his girlfriend Monica Vitale, leaving a hole in the centre.

