As they reached Hodel Street, they met a third man, Steve White. Steve worked at the nearby leisure centre and thought the initial sounds of gunfire were children throwing pebbles onto the building's roof. When he went outside to investigate, he witnessed the gunman firing on passers-by. Steve warned the other men of the danger and the trio cautiously crossed the street, approaching the bodies of Vesna, Gina and Robert. As they got close, the gunfire recommenced. John Muskat was struck six times in the left shoulder, chest, head, neck and right ear.

